\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we proposed SHAP-AAD, a two-stage framework that combines DeepSHAP-based channel selection with an efficient TCN for auditory attention detection using pure EEG signals. Our method effectively reduces the number of EEG channels while preserving high classification accuracy. Experimental results demonstrate that models using only 32 or even 8 selected channels for some specific cases can achieve performance comparable to the full 64-channel setup, validating the robustness and efficiency of our approach. 




