\caption{\label{fig:EV-CEnergy} The eigenvalues, denoted by "$+$" signs, of the SRG-evolved NN+3N-ind CS-Hamiltonian for the $^4{\rm He}$ system in $J^\pi;T=0^+;0$ state, computed with I-N3LO. Different colors depict the eigen-decomposition at different values of the $\hbar\omega$ parameter: blue for $20$ MeV, orange for $22$ MeV, green for $24$ MeV and red for $26$ MeV. The black dashed lines represent the continuum lines rotated by $~2\theta$, their intersection with $y$-axis is fitted from the different $\hbar\omega$ calculations, providing the many-body threshold energy consistent with the $N_{\rm max}$ of the calculation. Other parameters of the calculation are $\lambda=2.1\,{\rm fm}^{-1}$, $\theta=0.3$ rad, $N_{\rm max}=20$ and $N_f=12$.}
