\section{Conclusion}

The main challenge of PAPR reduction in HBR transmitters is the simultaneous consideration of both a limited band and a limited subspace for signal generation. Here we divided the problem correspondingly into two parts. Initially, the limited band property was employed and then we utilized a genetic algorithm to find the scaling coefficient for an LS-based solution to fit it into a limited subspace. Simulation results demonstrate the proposed algorithm for PAPR reduction in HBF has only $0.5dB$ loss compared to the bound achieved by convex optimization. The algorithm requires only $2$ iterations and its complexity is not much higher than the best possible, and there is a window to further reduce it.


