When $N$ and $M$ are $\Theta(T)$, \Cref{thm:non_preemptive_scheduling} results in $\O(T^3 \lg T)$ clauses, as opposed to the $\Omega(T^4)$ clauses of~\citet{mayankEfficientSATEncoding2020}.
