\vspace{-4em}
\abstract{This paper studies two estimators for Gaussian moment tensors: the standard sample moment estimator and a plug-in estimator based on Isserlis's theorem. We establish dimension-free, non-asymptotic error bounds that  demonstrate and quantify the advantage of Isserlis’s estimator for tensors of even order $p  >2.$ Our bounds hold in operator and entrywise maximum norms, and apply to symmetric and asymmetric tensors.} 

% REQUIRED
