\begin{proposition}\label{alpha=beta}
Letting $\psi_{\alpha,x_0}(x)=|x-x_0|^{\alpha}$ with $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $x_0\in \overline{\Omega}$. Then, one has
%{\color{green}{For $\alpha=1$, we have $L[\psi_{\alpha,x_0}](x)=0$, for every $x\neq x_0$.}} 
