\end{figure}

\subsubsection{Baseline Control}\label{sec:baselines}

As part of the baseline assessment, we conduct tests employing various $K_P$ and $K_I$ values without the integration of Eb-SbPGs, where the $K_P$ and $K_I$ values remain constant and not adaptable to system dynamics. This approach leads to challenges in determining the appropriate $K_P$ and $K_I$ values that would ensure system stability. The system exhibits pronounced oscillations and elevated overshoot, as depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:res_rand_gains}.
