\end{array}
\]

In our reduction, we define the countries as $\N = \{1,2\}$ where
\[V_1=\{x, a_i^2, a_i^3, a_i^5 \mid t_i = (x,y,z) \in T\} \quad \text{ and } \quad V_2= V\backslash V_1.\] 
The vertices from countries $1$ and $2$ are represented by circular and triangular vertices in Figure~\ref{fig:lintyk0c12s11n2}, respectively. We set $\segv_2 = 2$, and let $\segv_1\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}\cup\{\infty\}$, and $\sv_i\in \mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}\cup\{\infty\}$ for all $i\in \N$. 
Observe that the only $\Gamma$-cycles in the $\pG$ are those present within each gadget. Specifically, we define:
\[
