In the second scenario, our aim is to secure a specific area for a given time period. To achieve this, the quantity of interest (QoI) is defined to depend on the state \(u\). To create a meaningful scenario, we shift $
\Qoi_2:=\left\{(x,y)\in \Omega\, |\, 75\leq x \leq 125,\, 60 \leq y \leq 100\right\}\,.
$ upwards. Goal of OED 2 is to ensure that concentration values can be predicted correctly in region $\Qoi_2$ during the time from $\SI{5}{\s}$ to $\SI{12}{\s}$. This formulation results in the following operator:
 \begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
  \QoiO_2(\parameterfield)= \int^{\Tfinalqoi=\SI{12}{\s}}_{\Tzeroqoi=\SI{5}{\s}}\,\int_{\Qoi_2} \,\pts(\parameterfield)(t,\spacepoint)\,dt\,d\spacepoint= \int^{\Tfinalqoi=\SI{12}{\s}}_{\Tzeroqoi=\SI{5}{\s}}\,\int_{\Qoi_2} \,u(t,\spacepoint)\,dt\,d\spacepoint.
