where $\P(f)(a)=f(a)$ for every $a \in \P(A).$ We have to show that $\P(f)$ is well defined: as we saw before, if $a \in \Rad(A)$ then $f(a) \in \Rad(B)$, and so $f \colon A \rightarrow B$ restricts to $\P(f) \colon \P(A) \rightarrow \P(B)$.

