\subsection{Unified View}

Both data and model monitoring reduce to a common operation: comparing the distributions of two sample sets. Given two sets \( A \) and \( B \), where \( A, B \subset \mathcal{X} \) (input-based monitoring) or \( A, B \subset \mathcal{Y} \) (output-based monitoring), we define a general drift score:
\[
\text{DriftScore}(A, B) = \delta(P_A, P_B)
\]
This unified formulation supports monitoring across modalities such as imaging, structured EHR, and clinical notes, and is compatible with both static (between-site) and temporal (longitudinal) deployment settings.


