Synthetic data offer a promising solution to these challenges~\cite{chen2021synthetic}. They can increase dataset diversity by representing under-sampled populations or rare conditions, improving model robustness. Synthetic datasets also enable controlled simulations of data shifts, such as covariate, label, or concept drift~\cite{piano2022detecting}, to evaluate model behavior under varying conditions.

