\section{Lagrangian Floer cohomology}    

The Novikov field $\Lambda$ over a basis field $\mathbb{k}$ is   

\begin{equation}  
\Lambda\ \overset{def.}{=}\ \left\{\ \sum_{_{i=0}}^{^{\infty}}a_{_i}T^{^{\lambda_{_i}}}\ \bigg|\ a_{_i}\in\mathbb{k}, \lambda_{_i}\in\mathbb{R}, \underset{i\rightarrow\infty}{\lim}\ \lambda_{_i}=+\infty\ \right\}.    
\end{equation}    

Denoting by    

\begin{equation}  
\chi(L_{_o},L_{_1})\ =\ L_{_o}\cap L_{_1}  
\end{equation}  
the set of generators of the Floer complex, the latter can be defined as follows  

\begin{equation}  
CF(L_{_o},L_{_1})\ \overset{def.}{=}\ \bigoplus_{_{p\in\chi(L_{_o},L_{_1})}}\Lambda\circ p. 
\end{equation}  

For this to be a chain complex, we need to define the Floer differential and the $\mathbb{Z}$-grading of the Floer complex.    




