such that $e^{^1}$ coincides with the dual basis $e^{^1}\ \in\ \mathfrak{g}^{^\text{V}}$ via the identification $S^{^1}\rightarrow L_{_u}$ given by the  $S^{^1}$-action. 

This time, the holomorphic disks contributing to the equivariant Floer $A_{_{\infty}}$ algebras of $L_{_u}$. Those projecting on $[0,u]\ \subset\ [0,1]$ via $\mu$, and those projecting on $[u,1]\ \subset\ [0,1]$, with respective relative cohomology classes $\beta_{_1},\beta_{_2}\ \in\ H_{_2}(\mathbb{CP}^{^1}, L_{_u};\mathbb{Z})$.   



