whose dimension is 

\begin{equation} 
\left(\begin{matrix} &2n\\
&n \end{matrix}\right)-\left(\begin{matrix} &2n\\
&n+2 \end{matrix}\right)\ <\ \text{dim Im(ch)}.  
\end{equation}  

Denoting by $B=E_{_{\tau}}^{^n}$ the elliptic curve with complex multiplication, Lagrangian submanifolds with flat vector bundle do not generate a mirror of $D^{^b}(B)$.

\underline{Theorem}  
There is a cohomologically fully-faithful $A_{_{\infty}}$ functor for val$(\lambda)>0$ and $\lambda\neq\pm\sqrt{-1}T^{^{1/2}}$, 

\begin{equation}  
\boxed{\ \ \ \phi:\ {\cal F}_{_{\cal L}} \ \rightarrow\ \text{Br}({\cal W})_{_{\infty}}\  \color{white}\bigg]\color{black}}  
