The mirror correspondence induces an isomorphism of the cohomology vector spaces  

\begin{equation}  
\beta:\ H^{^{\bullet}}(B,\mathbb{Q})\ \xrightarrow{\sim}\ H^{^{\bullet}}(A,\mathbb{Q}). 
\end{equation}     

Lagrangian branes in $A$ with flat vector bundles cannot generate the mirror of $D^{^b}(B)$.  


To obtain the mirror of $D^{^b}(B)$, look at the mirror symmetry correspondence for $B=E_{_{\tau}}^{^n}$ more explicitly. For simplicity, $\tau=i$, such that $E_{_{\tau}}$ is a square torus. Consider a decomposition of the lattice  

\begin{equation}  
