We have a short exact sequence of $A$-modules
$$ 0 \rt L_i \rt F_i \oplus \Omega^i(k) \rt \cone(f_i) \rt 0, \quad \text{where $F_i$ is a free $A$-module}.$$
It follows that
$$\Tor^A_1(L_i, E)  \cong \Tor^A_1(\Omega^i(k), E) = k^{\mu(E)}. $$
Similarly we obtain
$$\Tor^A_1(L_i, E)  \cong \Tor^A_1(\Omega^i(X) , E). $$
So we have $\Tor^A_1(\Omega^i(X) , E) \cong k^{\mu(E)}. $
