\begin{abstract}
Inspired by Tokieda’s work on mechanical insights in geometry, 
we explore a hydrostatic approach to classical geometric problems. Using principles of fluid statics, we derive two mathematical results regarding polygons. These results illustrate how physical principles can assist in understanding mathematical identities.
\end{abstract}

